WEBVTT

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.041
He is, as of tonight...

00:00:04.918 --> 00:00:06.920
...a Triwizard champion.

00:00:34.865 --> 00:00:37.033
McGONAGALL:
This can't go on, Albus.

00:00:37.451 --> 00:00:40.203
First the Dark Mark. Now this?

00:00:40.454 --> 00:00:42.456
What do you suggest, Minerva?

00:00:43.665 --> 00:00:45.709
Put an end to it.

00:00:46.084 --> 00:00:48.086
Don't let Potter compete.

00:00:48.295 --> 00:00:50.797
You heard Barty. The rules are clear.

00:00:50.881 --> 00:00:53.800
Well, the devil with Barty
and his rules.

00:00:53.884 --> 00:00:56.344
And since when did you
accommodate the Ministry?

00:00:56.595 --> 00:01:00.599
Headmaster, I, too, find it difficult
to believe this mere coincidence.

00:01:00.849 --> 00:01:04.728
However, if we are to truly discover
the meaning of these events...

00:01:04.895 --> 00:01:08.356
...perhaps we should,
for the time being...

00:01:09.316 --> 00:01:11.610
...let them unfold.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.904
What--? Do nothing?

00:01:13.987 --> 00:01:15.864
Offer him up as bait?

00:01:16.865 --> 00:01:19.618
Potter is a boy, not a piece of meat.

00:01:20.494 --> 00:01:23.121
I agree. With Severus.

00:01:23.872 --> 00:01:27.834
-Alastor, keep an eye on Harry, will you?
-I can do that.

00:01:27.918 --> 00:01:32.756
Don't let him know, though.
He must be anxious enough as it is...

00:01:33.256 --> 00:01:35.926
...knowing what lies ahead.

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:38.929
Then again, we all are.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.933
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

00:01:53.777 --> 00:01:55.529
How did you do it?

00:01:56.947 --> 00:01:59.658
Never mind. Doesn't matter.

00:01:59.908 --> 00:02:01.785
Might've let
your best friend know, though.

00:02:01.952 --> 00:02:05.038
-Let you know what?
-You know bloody well what.

00:02:05.288 --> 00:02:07.749
I didn't ask for this to happen, Ron.

00:02:08.041 --> 00:02:09.793
Okay?

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.420
-You're being stupid.
-Yeah, that's me.

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:16.049
Ron Weasley,
Harry Potter's stupid friend.

00:02:19.928 --> 00:02:21.930
I didn't put my name in that cup.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:25.976
I don't want eternal glory.
I just wanna be....

00:02:27.936 --> 00:02:30.188
Look, I don't know
what happened tonight...

00:02:30.438 --> 00:02:32.274
...and I don't know why.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.775
It just did.

00:02:34.568 --> 00:02:36.069
Okay?

00:02:44.995 --> 00:02:46.788
Piss off.

00:02:57.966 --> 00:02:59.801
[FLASH BULB CLICKS]

00:03:01.803 --> 00:03:04.097
What a charismatic quartet.

00:03:05.473 --> 00:03:07.058
Hello.

00:03:08.018 --> 00:03:10.604
I'm Rita Skeeter.

00:03:11.062 --> 00:03:13.690
I write for the Daily Prophet.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:19.029
But of course you know that, don't you?
It's you we don't know.

00:03:19.487 --> 00:03:21.239
You're the juicy news.

00:03:21.489 --> 00:03:25.744
What quirks lurk
beneath those rosy cheeks?

00:03:25.994 --> 00:03:29.331
What mysteries do the muscles mask?

00:03:29.497 --> 00:03:32.834
Does courage lie beneath those curls?

00:03:33.001 --> 00:03:36.046
In short, what makes a champion tick?

00:03:36.463 --> 00:03:40.842
"Me, Myself & I" want to know.
Not to mention my rabid readers.

00:03:41.009 --> 00:03:43.386
So who's feeling up to sharing?

00:03:43.637 --> 00:03:45.764
Hm?

00:03:46.765 --> 00:03:49.267
Shall we start with the youngest?
Lovely.

00:04:01.655 --> 00:04:03.406
This is cozy.

00:04:04.074 --> 00:04:05.742
It's a broom cupboard.

00:04:06.076 --> 00:04:08.286
You should feel right at home, then.

00:04:08.536 --> 00:04:11.289
Don't mind if I use
a Quick-Quotes Quill, do you?

00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:13.083
Oh, no.

00:04:13.416 --> 00:04:15.377
So tell me, Harry.

00:04:15.543 --> 00:04:18.505
Here you sit, a mere boy of 12--

00:04:18.672 --> 00:04:20.090
I'm 14. Sorry.

00:04:20.298 --> 00:04:23.259
--about to compete
against three students...

00:04:23.426 --> 00:04:26.805
...not only vastly more
emotionally mature than yourself...

00:04:27.055 --> 00:04:29.516
...but who have mastered spells
that you wouldn't attempt...

00:04:29.683 --> 00:04:32.102
...in your dizziest daydreams.

00:04:32.519 --> 00:04:34.562
Concerned?

00:04:35.271 --> 00:04:38.566
I-- I don't know.
I haven't really thought about it.

00:04:38.775 --> 00:04:40.568
RITA:
Just ignore the quill.

00:04:41.111 --> 00:04:43.571
Then, of course,
you're no ordinary boy of 12, are you?

00:04:43.822 --> 00:04:46.324
-Fourteen.
-Your story's legend.

00:04:47.117 --> 00:04:49.202
Do you think it was
the trauma of your past...

00:04:49.452 --> 00:04:52.706
...that made you so keen to enter
such a dangerous tournament?

00:04:52.956 --> 00:04:54.582
No, I didn't enter.

00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:56.334
Of course you didn't.

00:04:58.712 --> 00:05:00.213
Everyone loves a rebel, Harry.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:04.134
Scratch that last.

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:07.595
Speaking of your parents,
were they alive...

00:05:07.804 --> 00:05:09.139
...how do you think they'd feel?

00:05:09.222 --> 00:05:11.057
Proud? Or concerned...

00:05:11.141 --> 00:05:15.061
...that your attitude shows, at best,
a pathological need for attention...

00:05:15.145 --> 00:05:17.856
...at worst, a psychotic death wish?

00:05:18.857 --> 00:05:23.987
Hey, my eyes aren't
"glistening with the ghosts of my past."

00:05:25.321 --> 00:05:27.157
[SCREECHING]
